AI Pharma — Docking_App
========================

This service builds on three open-source components:

1. AutoDock Vina (binary at bin/vina.exe)
   ----------------------------------------
   Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE_VINA).
   Source: https://github.com/ccsb-scripps/AutoDock-Vina
   Citations:
     - Eberhardt, J., Santos-Martins, D., Tillack, A.F., Forli, S. (2021).
       AutoDock Vina 1.2.0: New Docking Methods, Expanded Force Field,
       and Python Bindings. J. Chem. Inf. Model.
     - Trott, O., Olson, A. J. (2010). AutoDock Vina: improving the speed
       and accuracy of docking with a new scoring function, efficient
       optimization and multithreading. J. Comp. Chem.

2. Receptor PDBQT files (receptors/*_target.pdbqt and *_conf.txt)
   --------------------------------------------------------------
   Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE_DOCKSTRING).
   Source: https://github.com/dockstring/dockstring
   Citation:
     - García-Ortegón, M. et al. (2022). DOCKSTRING: easy molecular docking
       yields better benchmarks for ligand design. J. Chem. Inf. Model.

3. Meeko (Python ligand prep, pip dependency)
   --------------------------------------------
   LGPL-2.1 (consumed as binary wheel — meeko's source is NOT redistributed
   here). Used for SMILES → PDBQT conversion at runtime only. No source
   modifications.
   Source: https://github.com/forlilab/Meeko

All code under `app/` (FastAPI wrapper, Vina subprocess driver, schemas)
is original work by AI Pharma and is not part of any of the above projects.
